   "description": "The Tudor Black Bay 58 reference 79030N was introduced in 2018 and remains in current production. Collectors prioritize this model for its 39mm stainless steel case, which offers a thinner 11.9mm profile compared to the standard 41mm Black Bay line. It features a matte black dial with gilt accents, a unidirectional rotatable bezel with a red triangle marker, and the COSC-certified manufacture caliber MT5402, providing a 70-hour power reserve. The design references the 1958 Tudor Submariner reference 7924, positioning it as a vintage-inspired tool watch with modern technical specifications. On the secondary market, prices typically range between $2,800 and $3,600 depending on condition and whether it includes the \"rivet\" steel bracelet or a factory strap. While the 79030N is the core model, a notable production variation includes the \"Navy Blue\" 79030B released in 2020, which shares the same dimensions and movement."
